package engine

var delegationDescriptions = map[string]string{
	"spawn_agent": "Delegate a bounded task when authorized. Send independent spawns together. Foreground children in Collaborate run alongside the parent by default. Continue independent work after admission and use wait_agent when a step needs a result. Set overlap=false only if the very next parent step needs the child result. Outside Collaborate, set overlap=true to opt in. Overlapping children stay owned by this turn and completed results arrive automatically. Detached background work completes separately. Extra children queue at the concurrency limit. Keep the returned session and turn IDs.\n\n" +
		"Give the child the goal, scope and expected result. Include established findings and path:line references so its separate conversation can start with the remaining work. For a new child, follow the team instructions and pass the exact key of the role whose responsibilities fit. Omit role to use this turn's model when roleless delegation is allowed. Children inherit the worktree, mode and permissions. A named read-only role runs in Plan. Children cannot delegate. A registered worktree or disjoint file scope keeps parallel edits separate.\n\n" +
		"Use guide_agent for follow-ups. To explicitly continue verified unfinished work with spawn_agent in an idle child, pass its exact returned session ID and omit role to keep its role, model, worktree, settings and history.",
	"guide_agent":    "Give new directions to a child owned by this conversation using its exact session ID. A running child receives guidance at its next tool or model boundary and the call returns an admission receipt. An idle child starts a new foreground task with the same history, role, model, worktree and permissions, using current package settings. In Collaborate the parent and this new task proceed together. Use wait_agent for a dependent result. Queued or stopping children cannot be restarted.",
	"wait_agent":     "Collect a child's durable final answer and status within a bounded observation window. Launch ready children and finish independent work first. Wait only for a result needed now or for an explicit request to wait. Send independent waits together. A pending receipt refers to the same execution; do not repeat the spawn or poll it. Use the exact returned session and, when known, turn ID. New guidance returns early with guidance_pending so the parent can apply it.",
	"list_subagents": "Inspect this conversation's direct subagent sessions across turns. Returns session and turn IDs, assigned title and role, status, queued pause and stop_reason when recorded for that turn. Pass next_before back as before until null. Listing never resumes work.",
}
